.TH SILIGPU 1 "September 2026" "siligpu 1.1.0" "General Commands Manual"

.SH NAME
siligpu \- Apple Silicon GPU Usage Display Utility for macOS

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B siligpu
.RI [ OPTIONS ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B siligpu
is a CLI snapshot tool for Apple Silicon GPU usage via
.IR IOReport .
It samples GPU residency over a given interval, computes active percentage,
and exits — no continuous monitoring overhead. Does not require root privileges.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose mode (default).
Show detailed performance states.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-summary
Summary mode.
Show one-line summary (e.g.,
.IR "Usage: 10.25%" ).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-value\-only
Quiet mode.
Output only the numeric value (e.g.,
.IR "12.34%" ).
Ideal for scripts and status bars.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
JSON mode.
Output results in JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time " \fITIME\fR"
Time between samples.
Accepts plain numbers (milliseconds) or units:
.BR ms ,
.BR s ,
.BR m ,
.BR h .
Defaults to
.IR 1000ms .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B siligpu
Default (1 second interval, verbose output).
.TP
.B siligpu \-t 500 \-s
500 ms interval, summary mode.
.TP
.B siligpu \-\-time 2s \-q
2-second interval, value-only output.
.TP
.B siligpu \-\-json
JSON output.

.SH OUTPUT MODES
.SS "Verbose (default)"
.EX
GPU Stats / GPU Performance States
     OFF:                 776233 µs
      P1:                 216182 µs
      P2:                   6208 µs
   → Total active:        230625 µs (active)
          → Total:       1006858 µs (total)
          → Usage:         22.91 %
.EE

.SS "Value-only (-q)"
.EX
22.91%
.EE

.SS "Summary (-s)"
.EX
Usage: 1.64%
.EE

.SS "JSON (-j)"
.EX
{
  "usage_percentage": 46.06,
  "total_active_micros": 462027,
  "total_time_micros": 1003029,
  "states": [
    {"is_active": false, "name": "OFF", "residency_micros": 541002},
    {"is_active": true,  "name": "P1",  "residency_micros": 301833}
  ]
}
.EE


.SH INTEGRATION
.B siligpu
integrates perfectly with system fetch tools like
.IR fastfetch .
The
.B \-q
(value-only) flag combined with a short sampling interval provides clean
numeric output ideal for status displays.
.PP
Example
.I ~/.config/fastfetch/config.jsonc
configuration:
.EX
{
  "modules": [
    "os", "kernel", "terminal", "cpu", "gpu",
    {
      "type": "command",
      "key": "GPU Usage",
      "text": "siligpu -q -t 200ms"
    }
  ]
}
.EE

